{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Final rebar-debug report.\n\nRoot cause: _completion_precheck correctly read ticket state from a relocated tracker, but conflated the tracker parent with the code repository. It used that wrong root for completion-gate configuration and git commit evidence. Depending on files at the tracker parent, this either falsely rejected a valid referencing commit or silently treated the enabled close gate as disabled and closed unsigned.\n\nRepair: resolve code_root through config.repo_root(repo_root), while continuing to resolve tracker reads independently through config.tracker_dir(repo_root). Use code_root consistently for gate_enabled, referencing/file-impact checks, and completion verifier/autoresume repo_root and cfg_root. This avoids the LLM snapshot resolver because close needs the caller/current code checkout, not an attested material snapshot.\n\nHeld-out proof: tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_close_custom_tracker_root.py relocates .tickets-tracker outside the repo, enables the gate only in the code repo, creates/starts a ticket through REBAR_TRACKER_DIR, records file impact, creates a real trailer commit in the code repo, and closes through transition_cli. It passed and observed one verifier call, closed state, and certified signature. Exact-defect mutation back to tracker-parent derivation made the oracle fail because the verifier was never called even though the ticket closed; restoration returned GREEN.\n\nRegression sweep: completion-gate suite plus oracle passed 34 tests. The fixer also ran all lifecycle behavior tests (455 passed). make lint and make typecheck pass with the combined worktree."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787026216795956001,"uuid":"941694a1-b97c-491d-8029-fd83ceab58e8"}